### Summary — Exact Calls You Need

| Goal | Call |
|------|------|
| Get API-format prompt (to send to server) | `const { output } = await app.graphToPrompt()` |
| Get UI-format workflow (to save as .json) | `const { workflow } = await app.graphToPrompt()` |
| Get both | `const result = await app.graphToPrompt()` |
| Access a specific node's inputs | `result.output["3"].inputs` |
| Access a specific node's class type | `result.output["3"].class_type` |

**There is no `api.getPrompt()`.** The API object (`scripts/api.js`) has `queuePrompt(position, graphToPromptResult)` which receives the already-computed result. The graph-to-prompt conversion lives entirely on the `app` object.

